WEBVTT

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.120
R-Returned? To this town?

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.920
Yeah. Back when I was in college,

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.750
I thought of using a spell of resurrection
and a corpse that had been in use for 100 years

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.800
to create the immortal shikigami apparition
named Yotsugi Ononoki.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.510
That was exactly 15 years ago.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:29.020
And the phoenix found its next host
around then as well...

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:36.570
That's why he, the ashes that make up the first one,
gathered to this town right around then.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.270
That's what Big Sister here thinks happened.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.780
FIFTEEN YEARS AGO

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:44.780
<i>Speaking of 15 years ago,
there's one more thing I can associate it with.</i>

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.580
<i>Tsubasa Hanekawa became "Tsubasa Hanekawa"
sometime around when she was three years old.</i>

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.040
<i>Which means, that'd be
about 15 years ago, right?</i>

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.500
<i>Tsukumo-gami.</i>

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:56.960
<i>Phoenix.</i>

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.420
<i>Cat...</i>

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:04.090
<i>No, if I start saying that,
there's no need to focus soley on 15 years ago.</i>

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.140
<i>If that's the story, then you can think
of the time between 15 years ago and now</i>

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.930
<i>not as a specific moment,
but as a span.</i>

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.440
<i>As of 11 years ago,
lost on its way was... a snail.</i>

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.690
<i>Seven years ago,
a wish was granted by... a monkey.</i>

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.530
<i>Three years ago,
what took away some weight was... a crab.</i>

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.150
<i>Even the snake just two months ago
would fall under this category as well.</i>

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.160
It can't be...

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.660
All of the numerous stories of apparitions
that have been told in this town

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:30.080
ASH

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:33.330
are because that ash or whatever
came drifting along with the wind?

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.370
Of course not.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.340
Yoduru and company making Yotsugi
wasn't something that happened in this town.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:39.790
ASH COW CAT BEE SNAKE MONKEY

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.590
It's merely a distant cause.
I guess you can call it a suggestive code.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.260
Basically, all the apparitions
you've encountered are all your fault.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.350
You can't evade responsibility.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.220
However, during spring break,

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.730
the fact that Kiss-shot Acerola-orion
Heart-under-blade visited this town...

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:04.990
...definitely had something to do
with that ash.

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.280
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.620
SHINOBU MAIL, PART FOUR

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.120
You're speaking nonsense.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.250
And you call yourself the younger sister
of that Hawaiian shirt boy?

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.250
I MEAN, THAT'S NOT REALLY THE CASE

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.500
The reason I visited this country back then
was because I wanted to see Mount Fuji.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.550
But this mountain isn't Mount Fuji.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:29.260
This prefecture isn't Shizuoka or Yamanashi.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.050
Did you get lost on your way?

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.640
Or was it because three vampire hunters
were chasing you?

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:36.890
That's not it. You didn't get lost.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.900
You were guided here... to this town.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.770
Guided...

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.030
<i>What can I say. All of the things
that have tossed me around were...</i>

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.030
<i>...well, converging on this one man.</i>

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.700
<i>That manner in which
Gaen spoke was disgusting.</i>

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.620
<i>No. It's simply unpleasant.</i>

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.840
<i>What's with this feeling?
It's as if... I'm feeling jealous.</i>

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:03.420
Impossible.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:05.800
Such a thing is impossible.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.170
He died. He's dead.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:12.260
He wasn't persuaded by my words,
and threw away his own life.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.560
He's a huge idiot.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:17.180
What you're saying is nothing more
than a farfetched interpretation.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.350
Don't make fun of my lack
of a sense of direction.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.070
You seem to be asserting yourself
pretty strongly there, Shinobu.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:29.070
It's as if you'd be troubled if the man
who was the first one was still alive, you know?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:35.790
If your beloved slave was still alive,
and if he was about to be resurrected,

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.330
that would be cause for congratulations.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.460
CONGRATULATIONS

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.830
If anything, I can arrange a party
or something, you know?

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:48.760
Don't overstep your bounds, specialist.
Don't cross into a delicate area for me.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.590
What do you claim to know
about the events 400 years ago?

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.850
I know everything...

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.100
There's nothing I don't know.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.600
Changing the rendezvous point from the park
to the shrine has its appropriate reason as well.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.350
CHANGE —> NORTH SHIRAHEBI SHRINE

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.110
Can I ask one question, Ms. Izuko?

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.230
Sure, Ms. Suruga Kanbaru.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:13.620
Well, when this guy drifted into this town 15 years ago,
he was already basically just ashes, right?

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.620
Then, how, and with what catalyst,
did that cycle end,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.290
with him revealing himself to Araragi-senpai
as an armor-clad samurai like that?

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.960
What do you think is the reason,
Ms. Suruga Kanbaru?

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.300
I have no idea.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.590
But that reason has something to do with
why you changed the rendezvous point, right?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.340
You're sharp.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.720
You truly have talent
that's a shame to keep out in the wild.

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:43.850
I might only be thinking that
because I'm often consulted as a senpai.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:50.240
I do wish, Ms. Suruga Kanbaru,
that you'd support this upperclassman right here.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:50.820
TIMELINE

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.950
Fifteen years ago was when he -
the first one - came back to this town.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.870
He ended his wanderings, and drifted ashore
onto this town that was his homeland.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.750
He reached the goal of the tour of hell
that he felt was eternal.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.000
<i>Homeland?</i>

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:10.550
And every speck of ash that drifted in
gathered at the location that was the town's air spot,

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.130
right here, at the North Shirahebi Shrine.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.640
FIVE

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:16.640
FOUR

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.640
THREE

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:18.640
TWO

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.640
ONE

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:23.180
As you can see, this shrine has fallen into ruin.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.600
But of course, it wasn't always like this.

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:31.570
Fifteen years ago,
this shrine was still properly maintained.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.110
I heard it was a small, coherent, good shrine.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:39.780
In this case "small" and "coherent" aren't used
as an insult, but rather as a compliment.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.620
They had to keep it small and coherent.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.290
After all, this place is an air spot.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.670
An air spot for apparitions.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:50.670
Where they're likely to show up.
Where they're likely to gather.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.050
A location where "bad things" that aren't
full apparitions yet gather (shuuketsu).

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:57.050
And the location where apparitions
are terminated (shuuketsu).

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:01.720
If you sieze point after point like that,
and control each key location...

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:05.310
You can prevent accidents from happening.
You can avoid them.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:10.020
Big Brother Meme's job is to collect stories
of apparitions that have already happened.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.480
But the job of someone like me
is originally more along these lines.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.860
In other words, prevention, so that
things are stopped before they happen.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.200
On the other hand,
if those scattered spots,

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:23.160
the key locations, can't be controlled,
we can't prevent accidents.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.000
Because this was such a location...

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.000
"AIR SPOT FOR APPARITIONS"

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:32.380
...in the past, a famed onmyouji I can't even begin
to compare myself to created the shrine,

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:36.130
enshrined the god,
and went forth to maintain things.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:38.760
That had mostly gone well.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.010
The defense system was properly working.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.970
The "bad things" gathered here,

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:48.020
that become ingredients for apparitions,
were dispersed in moderation.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.900
There must've been a good god here.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.400
But everything has its limits.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:58.110
Let's see... Koyomin,
I hear you're prepping for college right now.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.160
If so, do you carry any talismans or anything?

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.410
Talismans.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.620
Do you know those things can expire?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:08.540
When the guardian note inside the bag rips,
the talisman expires.

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.670
It just means that even the most miraculous
of items doesn't have an infinite effect.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:19.220
This shrine, and the god enshrined in it,
reached their limits 15 years ago.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:25.930
But in that case, it's too harsh to blame
the shrine's caretaker, or even the enshrined god.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:28.060
It was completely beyond expectation.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:34.440
For the ashes of the first minion
of the legendary vampire to gather...

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.070
It reached its breaking point.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.440
Its limit.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:42.740
As a result, 15 years ago,
this North Shirahebi Shrine collapsed.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.700
Both in the occult sense,
and in the physical sense.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:52.210
To crush a shrine as ash...
Shinobu, your minion really is something.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.840
The fact that he was originally a specialist
probably has something to do with it.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.470
What's wrong, Koyomin?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.470
From the look on your face,
it seems like you understand.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.850
The other day,
when you time-slipped to the past,

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:09.140
you saw that North Shirahebi Shrine 11 years ago
was in far worse condition than it is now,

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.850
and I guess this inadvertently explained why?

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.650
That's right, that was his doing, the first one.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:19.280
The shrine that was supposed to
hold down the fort...

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.910
Couldn't hold down
the minion of the vampire.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:26.790
Just for reference, let me say
that there wasn't just one,

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.160
but two and three
attempts to renew this shrine.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:33.000
But an empty shrine with no god

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.790
has no constructive meaning,
even if it's all patched up.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:40.300
Each time they attempted a renewal,
it collapsed, broke, and fell into ruin.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:47.100
The nuisance was that Shinobu, or rather,
Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.390
and her minion, the first one,

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:54.810
have a power that draws apparitions to them
just by existing, like moths to a fire.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.940
That's what happened 11 years ago.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:04.320
When you two visited this shrine back then,
"bad things" filled these ruined grounds, correct?

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:10.080
I'm sure you were wondering why they had gathered
to such a density, but that's nothing special.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:15.460
It was what he, the first one - or rather, his ashes -
had gathered as the ingredients for an apparition.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.460
As ingredients... and as food.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.460
If I explain this much,

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:25.220
even without specialized knowledge,
you should have a good idea of what happened.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:30.720
Why the ashes of he, the first one,
escaped from the cycle of reincarnation.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:31.980
That's right.

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:34.440
If this shrine was
a "place that gathers easily,"

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.860
and the first one was
"an apparition that can gather easily"...

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:42.820
In other words, all the conditions
for an accident to happen converged here.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.610
Accidents overlapped.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:51.370
The first one, within the grounds of this shrine,
within the godless grounds of this shrine...

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.750
This whole time,
he kept eating in order to regain his stamina.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.000
The cycle of repeating ash and void now ended.

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:03.380
And what began would span the next 15 years...

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:06.010
A tragic tale of him finding revival.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:08.010
A tale of revival...

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:12.770
Perhaps this may have been
a tale of seeking revenge instead.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:22.900
Looks like this is a good time.
I finished up with most of the explanations.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:27.780
Koyomin, Shinobu, Ms. Suruga Kanbaru,
is there anything else you don't understand?

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:32.120
W-Well, there are so many more things
that I don't understand at all...

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.960
I-In the first place,
what should we do now?

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:39.460
What do you want us to do
to try to help your work—

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.290
I want you to take responsibility.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.050
Therefore...

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:46.680
I'll let you take it.
I'll let you inherit the responsibility.

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:49.430
You, Koyomin, and Shinobu.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:56.020
You said that, at first, you planned
for Ononoki to do this job alone.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:58.310
That this situation
exceeded your expectations.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:02.820
Then can you tell us
what the original plan was?

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:08.950
That's fine, but it's impossible to act out,
so it's kinda pointless to tell you.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:12.830
Do you remember why
Big Brother Meme came to this town?

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.950
It was because Shinobu came here, right?

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:18.120
I believe it was the same for Kaiki, too.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:23.210
As for Kagenui, I think she came here
because she heard the story from Kaiki.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:30.220
Right. Various specialists, all quirky and distinctive,
came to this town for similar reasons.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:33.600
But the reports of their investigations
came to me.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:34.850
EVEN STILL, I'M AMAZING.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:39.310
As a result of that, as the result of the close review
of the information submitted by each of them,

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:42.690
I came to understand
that there was a strange chain of events,

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.360
a certain situation,
happening in this town as of 15 years ago.

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:51.240
And so, I sent Yotsugi to this town once again.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:56.490
Her job was to clean up the ashes.
Simply put, cleaning up the shrine.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.870
<i>On the last day of summer break,
when she bumped into me in town,</i>

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:03.380
<i>she didn't seem to know what her mission was.</i>

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:07.960
<i>But after that, she was given a mission
that resembled the story of Cinderella?</i>

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:11.890
<i>But in the end, this means all of that failed, right?</i>

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.930
<i>Would Ononoki even fail a mission?</i>

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:19.600
<i>She's the one that saved
both my and Shinobu lives in one evening.</i>

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.390
<i>She's a diligent worker, you know?</i>

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:27.400
But Ononoki does have
a super-airheaded side to her as well.

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:29.530
Maybe there are times when she screws up.

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:32.660
You're talking as if
it has nothing to do with you, Koyomin.

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:35.780
Yotsugi's failure was you guys' fault.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.660
O-Our fault?

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.040
Can it be...

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:47.670
...that it has something to do with the fact that Shinobu and I
used the "bad things" pooled up in this air spot,

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:52.800
which had been sealed away by Oshino,
and was merely awaiting to be dispersed, as a source of energy?

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:58.310
IS THERE SOMETHING THAT COMES TO MIND?

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.560
Shinobu didn't do anything.

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:04.190
She didn't do anything...
She didn't have to do anything.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:07.320
It was enough that she came to this shrine.

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:12.950
Honestly, I don't know just how much
of the situation Big Brother Meme grasped.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:17.950
He doesn't speak much
and only reports the bare minimum.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:23.460
The only thing that's certain is that he used talismans
he had on hand to do some first aid on this shrine.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.880
Thanks to that band-aid treatment,

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:29.710
you could say we set it up
so that we cut off the first one's supply.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.970
But in such a situation of hunger, he...

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:38.350
Being cornered into an extreme case once again,
in such a mental state, he found out.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:42.850
He saw Kiss-shot Acerola-orion Heart-under-blade.

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.980
He witnessed her for the first time in 400 years.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:53.030
It was a one-sided observation.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:57.870
Shinobu, that was the first time
you came to North Shirahebi Shrine, right?

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:02.750
In other words... He found power
by seeing Shinobu for the first time in 400 years.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:06.620
That inspired the first one to rise up,
despite his body being nothing but ashes.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:10.630
And, even though he was in a state
of severe hunger, he revived himself?

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.010
Who said the situation was so romantic?

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.140
Simply put, an existence similar in nature
to another existence...

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:17.970
LIKE IT'S SOME TEEN ROMANTIC COMEDY

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:20.640
...showed up in a nearby location.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:25.770
The first one was affected by that,
and his apparition's nature swiftly became excited.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.360
That's why, when Yotsugi came here
after receiving the mission,

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:32.110
the North Shirahebi Shrine
was completely empty.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:34.860
After saying this much...

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:39.370
This time for sure, you know what the job
I want to ask you to do is, right?

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:41.740
It's to look for the first one.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:45.500
The first and the second one are both slaves,
so they should be drawn to one another.

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:50.500
If anything, the person to summon
first and foremost would be Kagenui, right?

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:55.510
Ononoki's master, the violent onmyouji
that specializes in immortal apparitions.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.380
I can't control her.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.640
I'd like her to lament for her entire life
that she has no opportunities to use her power.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:03.770
HINIKU NO TAN

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:07.890
But, well, I guess Ononoki is enough
for combat personnel, then...

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:08.650
Negative.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.570
At the point when I heard
the status report from Yotsugi,

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:16.780
in other words, at the point when I heard the report
that Koyomin had come in contact with the first one,

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:19.530
I called for one more assistant.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:22.160
I have to go pick him up pretty soon, too.

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:26.410
B-But, an assistant?
Isn't Ononoki enough for this?

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:27.710
She's not.

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.790
Big Sister here wants to settle the score
once and for all today.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:35.920
Now that he has a will, has a conscience,
and can arbitrarily use energy drains...

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:39.090
The longer we leave him be,
the stronger he gets.

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:41.300
The game keeps doubling up.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:44.890
If you take it easy,
he'll be completely revived.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.680
And if that happens,
he'll be impossible to control.

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:49.810
That will be the point when we have no choice
but to call for Yoduru.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:51.350
BIG MONSTER

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.320
<i>She speaks of Kagenui
like some inhumane weapon or something...</i>

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:55.940
No matter what,

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:59.450
I'd like to kill him...
before he eats a human.

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:07.950
Now, Big Sister will step out for a bit.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:08.410
5000 YEN

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:12.880
If you get hungry, you can use this
to go buy some breakfast, Koyomin.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.960
What are we going to do, Shinobu?

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.840
There's no ifs, ands, or buts.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:25.220
There was an irregularity, but from here on,
everything will go according to that specialist's plans.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:30.230
No matter what we do,
he'll be exterminated before the night is over.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:33.270
That's all there is to it.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:35.980
It's not something
we should do anything about at this point.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:40.650
There's the possibility he'll power up
if we get close to him.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:44.990
So unlike you, I probably won't see his face at all.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:48.370
This will all be dealt with without me.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:55.210
I'll tell you this. My master,
you shouldn't think of anything unnecessary.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:59.510
That woman may have said things
to rile you up for fun...

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:03.130
But for me, there is no "first" or "second"
in terms of my minions.

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:07.510
I've lived for over 500 years...
The order doesn't matter at all.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:12.390
The other day, when I told the story of the past,
did I not preface the story with instructions?

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.150
P-Preface?

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:16.150
Don't show worthless envy.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.030
Leave it at a cute level of jealousy.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.280
Don't be distressed.

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:23.530
Right now, you're the only one for me.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:34.790
<i>Given that I can't go home quite yet,
I can't afford to fast all the way till evening...</i>

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:40.760
<i>With the pairing with Shinobu severed right now,
I can't say I'm very resistant to hunger.</i>

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:43.170
<i>I can't let my underclassman starve, either.</i>

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:45.800
I request donuts.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:48.180
Should I go run over and get some?

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:52.980
No, I've hardly done anything up till now,
so I'd like to at least go do the shopping.

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:56.230
All right. Then I'll watch over Shinobu.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:59.860
I'll take care of Shinobu for you.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:06.870
<i>Is it all right to leave Shinobu and Kanbaru alone?
They've only just met.</i>

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:11.490
<i>But I can't go shopping toting Shinobu around
in this current situation.</i>

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:16.620
<i>Though it's safe because it's daytime,
I should have Shinobu stay put for now.</i>

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:18.630
Then, Araragi-senpai.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:22.210
Since you're going shopping...
I apologize for being rude,

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:25.130
but can I ask you to get something for me?

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.760
What is it? You can ask anything.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:32.270
I'd like you to buy a book.
It's a new book that's coming out today.

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.770
Coming out today? I see, that's fine.
Then, I'll go buy it for you.

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:38.650
It's a light-novel, so are you okay with that?

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.150
Come on now, that bothers me, Kanbaru.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:46.110
Do you think I'm one of those people that
treats light-novels like degenerate art or something?

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:51.030
I'm a high school boy that buys super-girly
shoujo manga with the cover facing up!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:54.580
I wouldn't think that
buying books would be embarrassing!

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:56.620
Hearing that reassures me.

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:57.920
So, what's the title?

00:18:58.210 --> 00:19:00.670
"Brutal Garçon Huff-Huffs a Half-Blood Boy!"

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:01.420
BRUTAL GARÇON HUFF-HUFFS A HALF-BLOOD BOY!

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:04.130
That's one of those light-novels
that aren't exactly light-hearted!

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:06.930
What kind of book are you asking
your upperclassman to buy you?

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:11.300
In the end, you're reading BL stuff...
And what's with that title?

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:11.510
BRUTAL GARÇON HUFF-HUFFS A HALF-BLOOD BOY!!

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:14.520
The title isn't everything for a novel.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:18.810
Lately, the world of literature has been
putting emphasis on the title as well.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:23.570
But past masterpieces often have a title that
makes you think it's nothing more than a vague idea.

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:23.820
BRUTAL GARÇON HUFF-HUFFS A HALF-BLOOD BOY!!
21ST BOOK

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:26.820
Well, it's true that a novel is about its contents.

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:29.700
But can the contents of that book
be something to look forward to?

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:35.200
Yes, it can. This one, the 21st book in the series,
is especially highly anticipated by the experts.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.200
923: NAMELESS EXPERT
NEW TITLE IS HERE
BRUTAL ASSAULT IS MY FAVORITE!
SO LOOKING FORWARD TO THE RELEASE DATE.

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:39.460
The series has gone on way too long!
And who are "the experts"?

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:44.210
In the newest installment,
the biggest mystery of the series since volume 1...

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:44.590
BIGGEST MYSTERY
"GRANDCHILD OF A 'GAL'?"

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:47.970
Whether or not the Brutal Garçon
is really "the grandchild of a 'gal'" will be revealed.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.260
He probably is the grandchild of a "gal"!

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:53.470
The author really dragged out
a mystery like that for 20 books?

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.600
Actually, the line I said
to you yesterday, Araragi-senpai...

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:57.850
"Eat up!"

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:01.690
That line was something I borrowed
from the main character of that series.

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:03.730
To think it was a line from a boys-love series...

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:04.610
I THOUGHT IT WAS CUTE!

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:09.070
You're not going to buy it for me?
Then I guess I'll just go home.

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:11.780
I'll buy it! You'll be satisfied if I buy it, right?

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:17.370
Oh, that's right... Araragi-senpai,
if you could, can you buy me a brassiere?

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:19.910
I can't do that, so I can't buy that for you.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:22.790
It's fine. I know you can do it, Araragi-senpai.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:26.760
Kanbaru, for some reason,
you expect too much from Araragi-senpai.

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:28.590
I don't care about the design.

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.510
You can use your aesthetic sense
to pick one, Araragi-senpai.

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:33.260
Don't ask me about my aesthetic sense
for picking out a brassiere.

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:36.510
I mean, there are all sorts
of designs for brassieres,

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:39.140
but in the end,
it's what goes in it that counts.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:40.890
Don't make it sound like a good line.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:45.270
I'm at my limit of being braless.
I really do want to cherish its contents.

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:48.900
You say "for some reason," but right now,
I just want to put a brassiere on.

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:51.200
Let's draw the line here.

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:55.660
<i>Here it is...</i>

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:58.700
<i>"Brutal Garçon Huff-Huffs a Half-Blood Boy!</i>"

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:01.040
<i>It's an amazing cover
that lives up to its title.</i>

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:01.250
BRUTAL GARÇON HUFF-HUFFS A HALF-BLOOD BOY!
(SECOND HALF)

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:03.170
<i>It is a bit embarrassing
to buy just these two books...</i>

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:05.420
21ST BOOK PUBLISHED!!
THE MYSTERY OF WHETHER GARÇON
IS A GRANDCHILD OF A "GAL"!
"EAT UP"
GARÇON SERIES 1-20 ON SALE!!

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:06.920
<i>I don't think it's manly to buy other books
as camouflage when buying certain books.</i>

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:08.800
BRUTAL GARÇON HUFF-HUFFS A HALF-BLOOD BOY!
(FIRST HALF)

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:15.850
<i>But in this case, I think it might be better
to hide the manliness instead.</i>

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:21.180
<i>Come to think, it's been a long time
since I was paired with Shinobu.</i>

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.730
<i>But because it was severed
by the "darkness,"</i>

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:28.780
<i>for the first time in a while,
I was acting alone in the true meaning of the phrase.</i>

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:30.320
<i>Taking my own course.</i>

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:31.440
<i>Freedom.</i>

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:35.620
<i>If so, can I take this momentary freedom,
without worrying about people's or apparitions' eyes,</i>

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.580
<i>this gap of lost time,
and make the most of it?</i>

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.580
IDOL - ACTRESS
PHOTO COLLECTION CORNER

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:42.080
<i>GRAVURE IDOL!
SLIGHTLY PERVERTED OLDER SISTER
SUPER-HOT PHOTO COLLECTION</i>

00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:48.090
<i>It seems that lately, because I've often
been having fun with Shinobu, Ononoki, and Hachikuji,</i>

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:50.800
<i>the suspicion that I have a Lolita complex
is growing day by day.</i>

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:54.050
<i>The times are the times,
the situation is the situation.</i>

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:57.470
<i>In order to clear me of any suspicion,
I need to employ the opposite strategy right now.</i>

00:21:58.220 --> 00:21:58.600
HOUSEWIFE PHOTO STUDIO
FULLY RIPE BODY, SPORTY MATURE LADY PHOTO COLLECTION

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:00.850
<i>In other words... Mature ladies!</i>

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:03.850
THE EMPLOYEES LAUGH

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:07.860
THE EMPLOYEES LAUGH

00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:12.070
THE EMPLOYEES LAUGH

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:15.200
THE EMPLOYEES LAUGH

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:27.460
Hey, second one.

00:22:35.970 --> 00:24:20.169
Were you able to relay my message to Kiss-shot?
